+---
+id: dl-002-applypatch-semantics-immutable-atomic-strict-own-properties-only
+type: decision-log
+title: "applyPatch semantics: immutable, atomic, strict, own-properties only"
+status: pending
+---
+
+<!-- decision-log body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold verbatim; `memory submit` replaces
+     these placeholder comments with real content and fills the required frontmatter fields. -->
+
+# Context
+
+`applyPatch` implements RFC 6902 on top of `resolvePointer` (RFC 6901). Services import it to change
+stored documents, so it must be predictable. The RFC leaves some outcomes open.
+
+# Decision
+
+- The input document and the patch are never mutated: the document is deep-cloned, and each `value`
+  taken from the patch is cloned on insertion, so the result shares no structure with either.
+- Atomic: any failing operation throws and no partial result is returned.
+- Invalid patches throw: non-array patch, non-object operation, unknown `op`, missing or non-string
+  `path`/`from`, missing `value` (add, replace, test), invalid pointer syntax.
+- Same strictness as `resolvePointer` (dl-001): own members only; canonical array indexes. `-` and
+  an index equal to the length are valid only for `add` (append).
+- `remove` and `replace` need an existing target; `remove` of the root throws; `replace` of the root works.
+- `move` from a location into its own child throws; `move` onto itself is a no-op (source must exist).
+- `test` compares deeply, ignoring member order; numbers, strings, `null` and booleans compare strictly by type.
+- A `__proto__` member is set as an own property (defineProperty), so it can never pollute prototypes.
+
+# Consequences
+
+- Callers pay a deep clone per call, in exchange for safety against aliasing.
+- `applyPatch` is pure and deterministic.
+- Errors are plain `Error`s with descriptive messages; no error subclasses exist yet.
